### ==========================================================
### SETTLEMENTS — la plata que va y viene con la gente con la
### que compartes gastos. Lo que te devuelven NO es income: entra
### a una cuenta, sin categoría, y fuera de Stats y de Budgets.
### Pagarle a otro SÍ es gasto tuyo: uno por línea, con su fecha.
### Un cobro se imputa SIEMPRE al gasto más viejo primero.
### ==========================================================
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = tester@test.com
@password = SecureP@ss123

# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###

@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### La cuenta por donde entra y sale (éxito)
# @name createAccount
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Bancolombia {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "type": "ACCOUNT", "balance": 5000000 }

###

@accountId = {{createAccount.response.body.id}}

### La categoría con la que se registra lo que le pagas a otro
# @name createCategory
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Salidas {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "type": "EXPENSE" }

###

@categoryId = {{createCategory.response.body.id}}

### El contacto y la salida
# @name createAna
POST {{baseUrl}}/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ana {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "color": "TEAL" }

###

@anaId = {{createAna.response.body.id}}

# @name createGroup
POST {{baseUrl}}/shared-groups
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Salida {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "contactIds": ["{{anaId}}"] }

###

@groupId = {{createGroup.response.body.id}}

### El gasto viejo, que es el que se cubre primero
# @name older
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 90000, "date": "2026-08-10T23:00:00.000Z", "description": "Cena", "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accountId}}" }

###

@olderId = {{older.response.body.id}}

POST {{baseUrl}}/shared-groups/{{groupId}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "transactionId": "{{olderId}}" }

### Y el nuevo
# @name newer
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 60000, "date": "2026-08-20T23:00:00.000Z", "description": "Taxi", "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accountId}}" }

###

@newerId = {{newer.response.body.id}}

POST {{baseUrl}}/shared-groups/{{groupId}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "transactionId": "{{newerId}}" }

### Ana te paga 30.000 — cubre el gasto MÁS VIEJO primero (éxito)
# @name collect
POST {{baseUrl}}/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "contactId": "{{anaId}}", "date": "2026-08-25T23:00:00.000Z", "collected": 30000, "accountId": "{{accountId}}" }

###

@settlementId = {{collect.response.body.settlement.id}}

### El movimiento de la cena ya cuenta 60.000, y su historial lo dice
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/{{olderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### El cobro, en la lista, como quinto tipo de movimiento
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?type=SETTLEMENT
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Stats no lo ve: lo que mide es lo que cuenta como tuyo
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/spending?groupBy=category&type=EXPENSE&from=2026-08-01T05:00:00.000Z&to=2026-09-01T05:00:00.000Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Un cobro en efectivo, fuera de la app — no mueve ninguna cuenta
POST {{baseUrl}}/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "contactId": "{{anaId}}", "date": "2026-08-26T23:00:00.000Z", "collected": 15000, "outsideApp": true }

### Un cobro con cuenta y «fuera de la app» a la vez — 400 VALIDATION
POST {{baseUrl}}/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "contactId": "{{anaId}}", "date": "2026-08-26T23:00:00.000Z", "collected": 1000, "outsideApp": true, "accountId": "{{accountId}}" }

### Un gasto que pagó Ana: ahí el que debe eres tú
POST {{baseUrl}}/shared-groups/{{groupId}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "Tickets", "date": "2026-08-12T23:00:00.000Z", "amount": 80000, "paidByContactId": "{{anaId}}" }

### Le pagas su línea — crea TU gasto, con la fecha de esa línea y tu categoría
POST {{baseUrl}}/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "contactId": "{{anaId}}", "date": "2026-08-27T23:00:00.000Z", "paid": 40000, "accountId": "{{accountId}}", "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}" }

### Pagarle sin categoría — 400 VALIDATION: la capa compartida no lleva categorías
POST {{baseUrl}}/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "contactId": "{{anaId}}", "date": "2026-08-27T23:00:00.000Z", "paid": 1000, "accountId": "{{accountId}}" }

### Pagarle más de lo que le debes — 400 SETTLEMENT_OVER_PAID
POST {{baseUrl}}/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "contactId": "{{anaId}}", "date": "2026-08-27T23:00:00.000Z", "paid": 900000, "accountId": "{{accountId}}", "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}" }

### Un cobro sin contraparte, o con las dos — 400 VALIDATION
POST {{baseUrl}}/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "date": "2026-08-27T23:00:00.000Z", "collected": 1000, "accountId": "{{accountId}}" }

### Escribir el quinto tipo a mano — 400: lo registra Settle up y nadie más
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "SETTLEMENT", "amount": 1000, "date": "2026-08-27T23:00:00.000Z", "toAccountId": "{{accountId}}" }

### Un gasto con invitados, para cobrarle al bloque
# @name party
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 230000, "date": "2026-08-18T23:00:00.000Z", "description": "Fiesta", "categoryId": "{{categoryId}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accountId}}" }

###

@partyId = {{party.response.body.id}}

# @name guestExpense
POST {{baseUrl}}/shared-groups/{{groupId}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "transactionId": "{{partyId}}", "split": { "mode": "EQUAL", "guests": { "count": 20, "name": "La oficina" }, "shares": [{ "party": "USER" }, { "party": "CONTACT", "contactId": "{{anaId}}" }, { "party": "GUESTS" }] } }

###

@guestExpenseId = {{guestExpense.response.body.id}}

### El bloque de invitados paga la mitad de lo suyo — se le cobra como a cualquiera
POST {{baseUrl}}/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expenseId": "{{guestExpenseId}}", "date": "2026-08-28T23:00:00.000Z", "collected": 100000, "accountId": "{{accountId}}" }

### Borrar ese gasto con el bloque ya pagando — 400 GUEST_BLOCK_HAS_PAYMENTS
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/transactions/{{partyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ana paga de más: 50.000 cuando ya no debe nada — queda a su favor
POST {{baseUrl}}/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "contactId": "{{anaId}}", "date": "2026-08-29T23:00:00.000Z", "collected": 50000, "accountId": "{{accountId}}" }

### Devolverle lo que pagó de más — quinto tipo SALIENDO, sin categoría y sin ser gasto
POST {{baseUrl}}/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "contactId": "{{anaId}}", "date": "2026-08-30T23:00:00.000Z", "paid": 50000, "accountId": "{{accountId}}" }

### Lo que ha ido y venido con Ana
GET {{baseUrl}}/settlements?contactId={{anaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Un cobro concreto
GET {{baseUrl}}/settlements/{{settlementId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deshacerlo — revierte sus movimientos y reimputa lo que quede
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/settlements/{{settlementId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deshacerlo otra vez — IDEMPOTENTE (200)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/settlements/{{settlementId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Un cobro ajeno o inexistente — 404 uniforme
GET {{baseUrl}}/settlements/019576a0-d7b6-7d6d-af6a-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
